### Example requests. Open in VS Code (REST Client extension) or PhpStorm and click "Send Request".
### Start the API first: composer start   -> http://127.0.0.1:8000
### All times are UTC. Asia/Almaty = UTC+5, so 10:00 Almaty = 05:00Z.
### Managers 1, 2, 3 are created by the seeder.
### Dates use Monday 2030-01-07 so they are always in the future.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### 1. Add a company -> 201
POST {{base}}/companies
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"name": "ТОО \"Алматы Трейд Компани\"", "bin": "170340021554", "phone": "+7 727 123 45 67"}

### 2. Same BIN again -> 422 "A company with this BIN already exists."
POST {{base}}/companies
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"name": "Duplicate", "bin": "170340021554", "phone": "+7 727 000 00 00"}

### 3. Second company
POST {{base}}/companies
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"name": "Digital Solutions", "bin": "180540012343", "phone": "+7 701 555 44 33"}

### 4. List companies with filter and pagination
GET {{base}}/companies?status=new&page=1&per_page=20
Accept: application/json

### 5. Book a meeting: Mon 10:00-11:00 Almaty -> 201
POST {{base}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"company_id": 1, "manager_id": 1, "starts_at": "2030-01-07T05:00:00Z"}

### 6. Same manager 10:30 -> 409 manager_busy (overlaps 10:00-11:00)
POST {{base}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"company_id": 2, "manager_id": 1, "starts_at": "2030-01-07T05:30:00Z"}

### 7. Same manager 11:00 -> 201 (back-to-back is not a conflict)
POST {{base}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"company_id": 2, "manager_id": 1, "starts_at": "2030-01-07T06:00:00Z"}

### 8. Company 1 with ANOTHER manager at 10:30 -> 409 company_busy
POST {{base}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"company_id": 1, "manager_id": 2, "starts_at": "2030-01-07T05:30:00Z"}

### 9. 17:30 Almaty -> 422 outside_working_hours (would end 18:30)
POST {{base}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"company_id": 2, "manager_id": 3, "starts_at": "2030-01-07T12:30:00Z"}

### 10. Saturday -> 422 outside_working_hours
POST {{base}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"company_id": 2, "manager_id": 3, "starts_at": "2030-01-12T05:00:00Z"}

### 11. Time without a timezone -> 422 validation_failed
POST {{base}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"company_id": 2, "manager_id": 3, "starts_at": "2030-01-07T10:00:00"}

### 12. Call "meeting_set" WITHOUT a meeting -> 422 (rule 5)
POST {{base}}/calls
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"company_id": 1, "manager_id": 1, "result": "meeting_set"}

### 13. Call "meeting_set" with the meeting from request 5 -> 201, company status = meeting_set
POST {{base}}/calls
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"company_id": 1, "manager_id": 1, "result": "meeting_set", "meeting_id": 1, "comment": "Agreed on a demo"}

### 14. Call "no_answer" -> 201
POST {{base}}/calls
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"company_id": 2, "manager_id": 2, "result": "no_answer"}

### 15. Reschedule meeting 1 to 15:00 Almaty -> 200, history keeps the original slot
PATCH {{base}}/meetings/1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"starts_at": "2030-01-07T10:00:00Z"}

### 16. Meeting with full history
GET {{base}}/meetings/1
Accept: application/json

### 17. Manager 1's schedule for Monday (Almaty day)
GET {{base}}/managers/1/schedule?date=2030-01-07
Accept: application/json

### 18. Cancel meeting 2 -> 200
PATCH {{base}}/meetings/2
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"status": "cancelled"}

### 19. Change a cancelled meeting -> 409 meeting_cancelled
PATCH {{base}}/meetings/2
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{"starts_at": "2030-01-08T05:00:00Z"}

### 20. Unknown meeting -> 404
GET {{base}}/meetings/999
Accept: application/json
